.TH WERKMEISTER-DOWN 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-down \- Stop containers, release slot, update proxy (use 'infra' for shared infra)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister down\fR [feature]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-volumes\fR
Also remove Docker volumes (node_modules, caches)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-features\fR
Stop and clean up all active features (ignores \e<feature> argument)
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBWhat it does:\fR
.IP 1. 3
Stops all Docker containers for the feature (\fBdocker compose down \-\-remove\-orphans\fR)
.IP 2. 3
Releases the slot back to the pool
.IP 3. 3
Regenerates the Caddyfile (removing this feature's routing rules)
.IP 4. 3
Reloads Caddy if running The feature's generated files (\fBcompose.yml\fR, \fB.env\fR, \fB.werkmeister/\fR) are left in place in its workspace — they're overwritten on the next \fBwerkmeister up\fR.
.PP
By default, per\-feature Docker volumes (node_modules, build caches) are preserved so the next \fBwerkmeister up\fR is faster. Use \fB\-\-volumes\fR to remove them for a full cleanup.
.PP
The command is safe to run even if the feature is already stopped — it will clean up any leftover state.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
